  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The use with ‘eyes’ identifies eyebrows specifically. The meaning of the clay structures in Job 13:12 is figurative and their precise shape is unclear. Gob and Gibbethon are place names. Gabbai is a Benjaminite in Nehemiah 11:8, but the text supplies no derivation of his name from the anatomical noun."
